From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erfan Abdi <erfangplus@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/25] apklayer: cond-signal-broadcast

pthread_cond_signal wakes every waiter: with one woken waiter an HWUI CommonPool task could be left queued while both workers slept, and the render thread then waited for its future forever (hang in HardwareRenderer.nSetStopped, 1 run in 10 of tests/vm/pendingintents.sh; 0 in 25 after). Spurious wakeups are allowed by POSIX, so waking all is always correct.

apklayer patch: step 10 of the former scripts/patch-bionic-translation.sh (see docs/PATCHES.md), patch 0015 of patches/bionic_translation.
---
 pthread_wrapper/libpthread.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pthread_wrapper/libpthread.c b/pthread_wrapper/libpthread.c
index b522a9d..a520418 100644
--- a/pthread_wrapper/libpthread.c
+++ b/pthread_wrapper/libpthread.c
@@ -644,7 +644,7 @@ int bionic_pthread_cond_signal(bionic_cond_t *cond)
 {
 	assert(cond);
 	INIT_IF_NOT_MAPPED(cond, default_pthread_cond_init);
-	return pthread_cond_signal(cond->glibc);
+	return pthread_cond_broadcast(cond->glibc); /* apklayer patch: see scripts/patch-bionic-translation.sh step 10 */
 }
 
 int
